2021.109708","year":2022,"counterion":"[Cl-].[Cl-]","record_id":"MLDB-001791","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicity of investigated dinuclear platinum(II) complexes and cisplatin was determined by measuring of partition coefficient using the “shake-flask” method in two phases system composed of n-octanol and 10 mM pH 7.4 phosphate buffer (containing 137 mM NaCl, 2.7 mM KCl). The absorbance of platinum(II) complex in the phosphate buffer was measured spectrophotometrically at a wavelength of its absorption maximum. The concentration of platinum complex was calculated from its extinction coefficient at absorption maximum that was previously determined."}]}